VPC Peering : A VPC peering connection is a networking connection between two VPCs that enables you to route traffic between them privately.
=============================================================================================================================================
VPC-1: VPC-A hosted in Virginia region
VPC-2: VPC-B hosted in Mumbai region

VPC-1
VPC Name: Proj-A-VPC-NV
CIDR: 10.0.0.0/16
Subnet Name: Proj-A-Pub-Sub-NA-1a
CIDR: 10.0.1.0/24
Internet Gateway: Proj-A-IGW-NV
Route Table Name: Proj-A-Pub-RT-NA
Subnet Name: Proj-A-Pri-Sub-NA-1b
CIDR: 10.0.2.0/24
Route Table Name: Proj-A-Pri-RT-NA

VPC-2
VPC Name: Proj-B-VPC-MU
CIDR: 20.0.0.0/16
Subnet Name: Proj-B-Pub-Sub-MU-1a
CIDR: 20.0.1.0/24
Internet Gateway: Proj-B-IGW-MU
Route Table Name: Proj-B-Pub-RT-MU
Subnet Name: Proj-B-Pri-Sub-MU-1b
CIDR: 20.0.2.0/24
Route Table Name: Proj-B-Pri-RT-MU

VPC --> Peering Connection

Name: VPC Peering from VPC-A to VPC-B
Select local VPC to peer with: Select VPC-A
Select another VPC to peer with: Select VPC-B & copy the VPC-B ID (for another region)

Accept the VPC peering connection at VPC-B(Mumbai) Peering connections

Update the Route Table of VPC-A with CIDR(20.0.0.0/16) of VPC-B & Select the Peering connection in Target.

Update the Route Table of VPC-B with CIDR of VPC-A(10.0.0.0/16) & Select the Peering connection in Target.

Now the resource can communicate privately.

