VPC Transit Gateway
====================================================================================================================================================================
VPC Transit Gateway: A transit gateway (TGW) is a network transit hub that interconnects attachments (VPCs and VPNs) within the same AWS account or across AWS accounts.

VPC-1: VPC-A hosted in Virginia region
VPC-2: VPC-B hosted in Mumbai region
VPC-3: VPC-C hosted in Mumbai region

VPC-3
VPC Name: Proj-C-VPC-MU
CIDR: 30.0.0.0/16
Subnet Name: Proj-C-Pub-Sub-MU-1a
CIDR: 30.0.1.0/24
Internet Gateway: Proj-C-IGW-MU
Route Table Name: Proj-C-Pub-RT-MU
Subnet Name: Proj-C-Pri-Sub-MU-1b
CIDR: 30.0.1.0/24
Route Table Name: Proj-C-Pri-RT-MU

N.Virginia --> VPC --> Transit gateway
Name: TG-Proj-A-NV

VPC --> Transit gateway attachments 
Name: TGA-Proj-A
Transit gateway ID: Select the ID which we created above step.
Attachment type: VPC
VPC ID: Select the VPC-Proj-A ID & associated subnets.

VPC --> Proj-A Route Table
Update the Route Table of VPC-A with CIDR(20.0.0.0/16) of VPC-B & Select the Transit Gateway in Target.
Update the Route Table of VPC-A with CIDR(30.0.0.0/16) of VPC-C & Select the Transit Gateway in Target.

Mumbia --> VPC --> Transit gateway
Name: TG-Proj-B and Proj-C-MU

VPC --> Transit gateway attachments 
Name: TGA-Proj-B 
Transit gateway ID: Select the ID which we created above step.
Attachment type: VPC
VPC ID: Select the VPC-Proj-B ID & associated subnets

Name: TGA-Proj-C
Transit gateway ID: Select the ID which we created above step.
Attachment type: VPC
VPC ID: Select the VPC-Proj-C ID & associated subnets

VPC --> Proj-B Route Table
Update the Route Table of VPC-B with CIDR(10.0.0.0/16) of VPC-A & Select the Transit Gateway in Target.
Update the Route Table of VPC-B with CIDR(30.0.0.0/16) of VPC-C & Select the Transit Gateway in Target.

VPC --> Proj-C Route Table
Update the Route Table of VPC-C with CIDR(10.0.0.0/16) of VPC-A & Select the Transit Gateway in Target.
Update the Route Table of VPC-C with CIDR(20.0.0.0/16) of VPC-B & Select the Transit Gateway in Target.

Below steps are needed only if we need connectivity b/t VPC's which are hosted on different regions.

Mumbai --> VPC --> Transit gateway attachments
Name: TGA-VPC-Peering-MU-to-NV
Transit gateway ID: Select the ID which we created above step.
Attachment type: Peering Connection
Region: Select N.Virginia
Transit gateway (accepter): Copy and paste the Transit Gateway ID from N.Virginia.

N.Virginia --> VPC --> Transit gateway attachments
Accept the peering connection at VPC-A(N.Virginia)

VPC --> Transit gateway route tables
Select the Route table associated to Transit Gateway
routes --> create static route
Update the CIDR of VPC-B(20.0.0.0/16) and select Transit Gateway Peering
Update the CIDR of VPC-C(30.0.0.0/16) and select Transit Gateway Peering

Mumbai --> VPC --> Transit gateway route tables
Select the Route table associated to Transit Gateway
routes --> create static route
Update the CIDR of VPC-A(10.0.0.0/16) and select Transit Gateway Peering
